text: ['({T}: Add {B}.)', '({T}: Add {G}.)', '({T}: Add {R}.)', '({T}: Add {U}.)', '({T}: Add {W}.)', 'Add {B}{B}{B}.', 'All Sliver creatures get +1/+1.', 'All Sliver creatures have "{2}: This creature gets +0/+1 until end of turn."', 'All Sliver creatures have "{2}: This creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn."', 'All Sliver creatures have flying.', 'All Sliver creatures have trample.', 'All Slivers have "Pay 2 life: Return this permanent to its owner\'s hand."', 'All Slivers have "{2}, Sacrifice this permanent: Draw a card."', 'All Slivers have "{2}, Sacrifice this permanent: This permanent deals 2 damage to any target."', 'All Slivers have "{2}, Sacrifice this permanent: You gain 4 life."', 'All Slivers have "{2}: Regenerate this permanent."', "All Slivers have shroud. (They can't be the targets of spells or abilities.)", 'All creatures lose all abilities and have base power and toughness 1/1.', 'All damage that would be dealt this turn to target creature you control by a source of your choice is dealt to another target creature instead.', 'Any player may cast creature spells with mana value 3 or less without paying their mana costs and as though they had flash.', "As Volrath's Laboratory enters the battlefield, choose a color and a creature type.\\n{5}, {T}: Create a 2/2 creature token of the chosen color and type.", 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a land.\\nSearch your library for up to two basic land cards, put them onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', "At the beginning of each player's upkeep, that player chooses target player who controls more creatures than they do and is their opponent. The first player may reveal cards from the top of their library until they reveal a creature card. If the first player does, that player puts that card onto the battlefield and all other cards revealed this way into their graveyard.", 'At the beginning of each upkeep, create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token.', 'At the beginning of your end step, you may reveal your hand and put all land cards from it onto the battlefield. If you do, discard your hand.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, Jinxed Idol deals 2 damage to you.\\nSacrifice a creature: Target opponent gains control of Jinxed Idol.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, if there are no Reflection tokens on the battlefield, create a 2/2 white Reflection creature token.\\n{0}: Destroy target Reflection.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, tap Carnophage unless you pay 1 life.', "At the beginning of your upkeep, you may put a treasure counter on Legacy's Allure.\\nSacrifice Legacy's Allure: Gain control of target creature with power less than or equal to the number of treasure counters on Legacy's Allure. (This effect lasts indefinitely.)", 'Buyback {2} (You may pay an additional {2} as you cast this spell. If you do, put this card into your hand as it resolves.)\\nReturn the top creature card of your graveyard to the battlefield. That creature gains haste until end of turn. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step.', "Buyback {3} (You may pay an additional {3} as you cast this spell. If you do, put this card into your hand as it resolves.)\\nEvincar's Justice deals 2 damage to each creature and each player.", 'Buyback {3} (You may pay an additional {3} as you cast this spell. If you do, put this card into your hand as it resolves.)\\nFanning the Flames deals X damage to any target.', 'Buyback {3} (You may pay an additional {3} as you cast this spell. If you do, put this card into your hand as it resolves.)\\nPrevent the next 3 damage that would be dealt to target creature this turn.', "Buyback {3} (You may pay an additional {3} as you cast this spell. If you do, put this card into your hand as it resolves.)\\nReturn target permanent to its owner's hand.", 'Buyback {3} (You may pay an additional {3} as you cast this spell. If you do, put this card into your hand as it resolves.)\\nTarget creature gets +3/+0 until end of turn.', "Buyback {3} (You may pay an additional {3} as you cast this spell. If you do, put this card into your hand as it resolves.)\\nTarget land becomes a 2/2 creature that's still a land. (This effect lasts indefinitely.)", 'Buyback {4} (You may pay an additional {4} as you cast this spell. If you do, put this card into your hand as it resolves.)\\nCreate a 1/1 black Rat creature token.', 'Buyback {4} (You may pay an additional {4} as you cast this spell. If you do, put this card into your hand as it resolves.)\\nSearing Touch deals 1 damage to any target.', 'Buyback {4} (You may pay an additional {4} as you cast this spell. If you do, put this card into your hand as it resolves.)\\nTarget creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Buyback {5} (You may pay an additional {5} as you cast this spell. If you do, put this card into your hand as it resolves.)\\nDraw a card.', 'Buyback—Discard two cards. (You may discard two cards in addition to any other costs as you cast this spell. If you do, put this card into your hand as it resolves.)\\nCounter target spell.', 'Buyback—Sacrifice a land. (You may sacrifice a land in addition to any other costs as you cast this spell. If you do, put this card into your hand as it resolves.)\\nCreate a 1/1 white Pegasus creature token with flying.', 'Caldera Lake enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {R}. Caldera Lake deals 1 damage to you.', 'Cast this spell only during your end step.\\nAs an additional cost to cast this spell, pay X life.\\nDraw X cards.', 'Choose two target creatures controlled by the same player. Exile one of those creatures and put two +1/+1 counters on the other.', 'Counter target spell unless its controller pays {3}.', "Counter target spell with mana value X. (For example, if that spell's mana cost is {3}{U}{U}, X is 5.)", 'Counter target spell.', 'Counter target spell.\\nDraw a card.', "Craven Giant can't block.", 'Creatures you control get +3/+3 and gain trample until end of turn.', "Crovax the Cursed enters the battlefield with four +1/+1 counters on it.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you may sacrifice a creature. If you do, put a +1/+1 counter on Crovax. If you don't, remove a +1/+1 counter from Crovax.\\n{B}: Crovax gains flying until end of turn.", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nWall of Diffusion can block creatures with shadow as though Wall of Diffusion had shadow.", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nWhenever Wall of Essence is dealt combat damage, you gain that much life.", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nWhenever Wall of Souls is dealt combat damage, it deals that much damage to target opponent or planeswalker.", 'Defender\\nWhen Wall of Blossoms enters the battlefield, draw a card.', 'Destroy all creatures target player controls. For each creature that died this way, that player creates two 1/1 red Goblin creature tokens.', "Destroy all creatures that aren't enchanted. They can't be regenerated.", 'Destroy all enchantments.', 'Destroy target artifact or enchantment.', 'Destroy target artifact, creature, or land. Aftershock deals 3 damage to you.', 'Destroy target artifact.', 'Destroy target blocked creature.', "Destroy target nonblack creature. It can't be regenerated.", 'Destroy target tapped creature.', 'Discard a card: Regenerate Patchwork Gnomes. (The next time this creature would be destroyed, instead tap it, remove it from combat, and heal all damage on it.)', 'Discard a card: Thalakos Drifters gains shadow until end of turn. (It can block or be blocked by only creatures with shadow.)', 'Discard a creature card: Vampire Hounds gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Distribute two +1/+1 counters among one or two target creatures.', 'Draw four cards. You skip your next turn.', 'Draw three cards, then discard a card.', "Dream Prowler can't be blocked as long as it's attacking alone.", 'Each creature gets +1/+1 for each other creature on the battlefield that shares at least one creature type with it. (For example, if two Goblin Warriors and a Goblin Shaman are on the battlefield, each gets +2/+2.)', 'Each player chooses from among the permanents they control an artifact, a creature, an enchantment, and a land, then sacrifices the rest.', 'Each player exiles all creature cards from their graveyard, then sacrifices all creatures they control, then puts all cards they exiled this way onto the battlefield.', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't attack or block, and its activated abilities can't be activated. That creature's controller may sacrifice a permanent for that player to ignore this effect until end of turn.\\n{1}{U}: Return Volrath's Curse to its owner's hand.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't attack or block.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature doesn't untap during its controller's untap step.\\n{W}: Return Shackles to its owner's hand.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+3.\\n{W}: Return Conviction to its owner's hand.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+2 and can't block.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +3/+3.\\nWhen enchanted creature becomes the target of a spell or ability, destroy that creature. It can't be regenerated.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets -1/-1 and has fear. (It can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or black creatures.)", 'Enchant creature\\nPrevent all combat damage that would be dealt to and dealt by enchanted creature.', 'Enchant creature\\nWhenever enchanted creature deals damage to an opponent, you may draw a card.', 'Enchant creature\\n{R}: Enchanted creature gets +1/-1 until end of turn.', 'Exchange control of target artifact or creature and another target permanent that shares one of those types with it. (This effect lasts indefinitely.)', "Fear (This creature can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or black creatures.)\\nWhen Commander Greven il-Vec enters the battlefield, sacrifice a creature.", 'First strike', 'First strike (This creature deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.)\\n{R}: Sandstone Warrior gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', "First strike, forestwalk, vigilance (This creature deals combat damage before creatures without first strike, it can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Forest, and attacking doesn't cause this creature to tap.)", "First strike, protection from black and from red (This creature deals combat damage before creatures without first strike. It can't be blocked, targeted, dealt damage, or enchanted by anything black or red.)", 'First strike\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, if your opponents control no creatures, Kezzerdrix deals 4 damage to you.', 'First strike\\nWhenever Renegade Warlord attacks, each other attacking creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', "Flame Wave deals 4 damage to target player or planeswalker and each creature that player or that planeswalker's controller controls.", 'Flying', "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nSacrifice Shard Phoenix: It deals 2 damage to each creature without flying.\\n{R}{R}{R}: Return Shard Phoenix from your graveyard to your hand. Activate only during your upkeep.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nWhen Rathi Dragon enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you sacrifice two Mountains.", 'Flying, first strike', "Flying\\nAs Dracoplasm enters the battlefield, sacrifice any number of creatures. Dracoplasm's power becomes the total power of those creatures and its toughness becomes their total toughness.\\n{R}: Dracoplasm gets +1/+0 until end of turn.", "Flying\\nDiscard a card: Return Ephemeron to its owner's hand.", 'Flying\\nDiscard a creature card: Skyshroud Vampire gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', "Flying\\nExalted Dragon can't attack unless you sacrifice a land. (This cost is paid as attackers are declared.)", "Flying\\nPay 2 life: Return Selenia, Dark Angel to its owner's hand.", "Flying\\nRevenant's power and toughness are each equal to the number of creature cards in your graveyard.", 'Flying\\nThopter Squadron enters the battlefield with three +1/+1 counters on it.\\n{1}, Remove a +1/+1 counter from Thopter Squadron: Create a 1/1 colorless Thopter artifact creature token with flying. Activate only as a sorcery.\\n{1}, Sacrifice another Thopter: Put a +1/+1 counter on Thopter Squadron. Activate only as a sorcery.', "Flying\\nWhen Avenging Angel dies, you may put it on top of its owner's library.", 'Flying\\nWhenever Angelic Protector becomes the target of a spell or ability, Angelic Protector gets +0/+3 until end of turn.', 'Flying\\n{0}: The next 1 damage that would be dealt to Spirit en-Kor this turn is dealt to target creature you control instead.', 'Flying\\n{1}{B}: Regenerate Screeching Harpy.', 'Flying\\n{B}: Dungeon Shade gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Flying\\n{R}: Flowstone Wyvern gets +2/-2 until end of turn.', "Flying\\n{T}, Tap two untapped creatures you control: Return target permanent to its owner's hand.", 'Flying\\n{T}: Mawcor deals 1 damage to any target.', 'Flying\\n{T}: Target creature gains flying until end of turn.', 'Flying\\n{U}: Change the target of target spell or ability that targets only Silver Wyvern. The new target must be a creature.', "Flying\\n{U}: Put Wayward Soul on top of its owner's library.", "Hammerhead Shark can't attack unless defending player controls an Island.", 'Heartwood Dryad can block creatures with shadow as though Heartwood Dryad had shadow.', "If Mox Diamond would enter the battlefield, you may discard a land card instead. If you do, put Mox Diamond onto the battlefield. If you don't, put it into its owner's graveyard.\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color.", 'Kindle deals X damage to any target, where X is 2 plus the number of cards named Kindle in all graveyards.', 'Krakilin enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it.\\n{1}{G}: Regenerate Krakilin.', 'Lightning Blast deals 4 damage to any target.', "Magmasaur enters the battlefield with five +1/+1 counters on it.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you may remove a +1/+1 counter from Magmasaur. If you don't, sacrifice Magmasaur and it deals damage equal to the number of +1/+1 counters on it to each creature without flying and each player.", 'Mindless Automaton enters the battlefield with two +1/+1 counters on it.\\n{1}, Discard a card: Put a +1/+1 counter on Mindless Automaton.\\nRemove two +1/+1 counters from Mindless Automaton: Draw a card.', "Mogg Conscripts can't attack unless you've cast a creature spell this turn.", "Mogg Flunkies can't attack or block alone.", "Mountainwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Mountain.)", 'Needle Storm deals 4 damage to each creature with flying.', 'Pine Barrens enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {G}. Pine Barrens deals 1 damage to you.', 'Prevent the next 1 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.\\nDraw a card.', 'Protection from black\\nShadow (This creature can block or be blocked by only creatures with shadow.)', 'Protection from red\\nShadow (This creature can block or be blocked by only creatures with shadow.)', 'Put target creature card from a graveyard onto the battlefield under your control. You lose life equal to its mana value.', "Put target creature on top of its owner's library.", 'Rather than pay the mana cost for a spell, its controller may discard a card that shares a color with that spell.', 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)', 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)\\n{W}: Mounted Archers can block an additional creature this turn.', 'Return two target creature cards from your graveyard to your hand.', 'Reveal the top four cards of your library. Put all land cards revealed this way into your hand and the rest into your graveyard.', 'Rolling Thunder deals X damage divided as you choose among any number of targets.', 'Sacrifice Bottle Gnomes: You gain 3 life.', 'Sacrifice Mogg Fanatic: It deals 1 damage to any target.', 'Sacrifice Skyshaper: Creatures you control gain flying until end of turn.', "Sacrifice a creature, Return Recurring Nightmare to its owner's hand: Return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield. Activate only as a sorcery.", 'Sacrifice a creature: Goblin Bombardment deals 1 damage to any target.', 'Salt Flats enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {B}. Salt Flats deals 1 damage to you.', 'Scabland enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {W}. Scabland deals 1 damage to you.', "Sea Monster can't attack unless defending player controls an Island.", 'Search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for three cards and reveal them. Target opponent chooses one. Put that card into your hand and the rest into your graveyard. Then shuffle.', 'Shadow (This creature can block or be blocked by only creatures with shadow.)', "Shadow (This creature can block or be blocked by only creatures with shadow.)\\nDauthi Horror can't be blocked by white creatures.", 'Shadow (This creature can block or be blocked by only creatures with shadow.)\\nDauthi Slayer attacks each combat if able.', "Shadow (This creature can block or be blocked by only creatures with shadow.)\\nDauthi Warlord's power is equal to the number of creatures with shadow on the battlefield.", "Shadow (This creature can block or be blocked by only creatures with shadow.)\\nDiscard a card: Return Thalakos Scout to its owner's hand.", "Shadow (This creature can block or be blocked by only creatures with shadow.)\\nSoltari Lancer has first strike as long as it's attacking.", 'Shadow (This creature can block or be blocked by only creatures with shadow.)\\nWhen Thalakos Seer leaves the battlefield, draw a card.', 'Shadow (This creature can block or be blocked by only creatures with shadow.)\\nWhenever Soltari Champion attacks, other creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Shadow (This creature can block or be blocked by only creatures with shadow.)\\nWhenever Soltari Trooper attacks, it gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Shadow (This creature can block or be blocked by only creatures with shadow.)\\n{0}: The next time Soltari Guerrillas would deal combat damage to an opponent this turn, it deals that damage to target creature instead.', 'Shadow (This creature can block or be blocked by only creatures with shadow.)\\n{B}{B}, Sacrifice Dauthi Jackal: Destroy target blocking creature.', 'Shadowstorm deals 2 damage to each creature with shadow.', 'Skip your draw step.\\nWhenever you play a card, draw a card.\\nYour maximum hand size is two.', 'Skyshroud Forest enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {U}. Skyshroud Forest deals 1 damage to you.', 'Spike Breeder enters the battlefield with three +1/+1 counters on it.\\n{2}, Remove a +1/+1 counter from Spike Breeder: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.\\n{2}, Remove a +1/+1 counter from Spike Breeder: Create a 1/1 green Spike creature token.', 'Spike Colony enters the battlefield with four +1/+1 counters on it.\\n{2}, Remove a +1/+1 counter from Spike Colony: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.', 'Spike Feeder enters the battlefield with two +1/+1 counters on it.\\n{2}, Remove a +1/+1 counter from Spike Feeder: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.\\nRemove a +1/+1 counter from Spike Feeder: You gain 2 life.', 'Spike Hatcher enters the battlefield with six +1/+1 counters on it.\\n{2}, Remove a +1/+1 counter from Spike Hatcher: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.\\n{1}, Remove a +1/+1 counter from Spike Hatcher: Regenerate Spike Hatcher.', 'Spitting Hydra enters the battlefield with four +1/+1 counters on it.\\n{1}{R}, Remove a +1/+1 counter from Spitting Hydra: It deals 1 damage to target creature.', 'Tap an untapped creature you control: Telethopter gains flying until end of turn.', 'Tap target creature. It deals damage equal to its power to another target creature.', 'Target blocking creature gets +4/+4 until end of turn.\\nDraw a card.', "Target creature can't block this turn.\\nDraw a card.", 'Target creature deals damage to itself equal to its power.', 'Target creature gains shadow until end of turn. (It can block or be blocked by only creatures with shadow.)\\nDraw a card.', "Target creature gets +3/+3 and gains flying until end of turn. (It can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)", 'Target creature loses shadow until end of turn.\\nDraw a card.', 'Target opponent reveals their hand. You choose a card from it. That player discards that card.', 'Target player discards three cards.', 'Target player sacrifices a creature.', 'Target player takes an extra turn after this one.', "Trample (This creature can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)", 'Trample\\n{1}{G}: Regenerate Carnassid.', 'Trample\\n{R}: Flowstone Mauler gets +1/-1 until end of turn.', "Untap target creature you don't control. That creature blocks this turn if able.\\nDraw a card.", 'Vigilance', 'When Anarchist enters the battlefield, you may return target sorcery card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Gravedigger enters the battlefield, you may return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Sarcomancy enters the battlefield, create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, if there are no Zombies on the battlefield, Sarcomancy deals 1 damage to you.', 'When Scrivener enters the battlefield, you may return target instant card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Serpent Warrior enters the battlefield, you lose 3 life.', 'When Staunch Defenders enters the battlefield, you gain 4 life.', 'When you control a creature with toughness 2 or less, sacrifice Endangered Armodon.', 'When you play another land, sacrifice City of Traitors.\\n{T}: Add {C}{C}.', 'Whenever Charging Paladin attacks, it gets +0/+3 until end of turn.', 'Whenever Crashing Boars attacks, defending player chooses an untapped creature they control. That creature blocks Crashing Boars this turn if able.', 'Whenever Lowland Basilisk deals damage to a creature, destroy that creature at end of combat.', 'Whenever Mogg Maniac is dealt damage, it deals that much damage to target opponent or planeswalker.', 'Whenever a Sliver becomes blocked, that Sliver gets +1/+1 until end of turn for each creature blocking it.', "Whenever a creature enters the battlefield, that creature's controller may have it deal damage equal to its power to any target of their choice.", "Whenever a creature is dealt damage, destroy it. It can't be regenerated.", 'Whenever a nontoken creature is put into your graveyard from the battlefield, create a 1/1 white Spirit creature token with flying.', 'Whenever a player casts a spell, Spellshock deals 2 damage to that player.', 'You may choose not to untap Coffin Queen during your untap step.\\n{2}{B}, {T}: Put target creature card from a graveyard onto the battlefield under your control. When Coffin Queen becomes untapped or you lose control of Coffin Queen, exile that creature.', 'You may tap or untap target artifact, creature, or land.\\nDraw a card.', '{0}: The next 1 damage that would be dealt to Nomads en-Kor this turn is dealt to target creature you control instead.', '{0}: The next 1 damage that would be dealt to Shaman en-Kor this turn is dealt to target creature you control instead.\\n{1}{W}: The next time a source of your choice would deal damage to target creature this turn, that damage is dealt to Shaman en-Kor instead.', '{0}: The next 1 damage that would be dealt to Warrior en-Kor this turn is dealt to target creature you control instead.', "{1}, {T}: Return target creature to its owner's hand unless its controller pays {1}.", "{1}{B}, Sacrifice Thrull Surgeon: Look at target player's hand and choose a card from it. That player discards that card. Activate only as a sorcery.", '{1}{G}: Regenerate Skyshroud Troll.', '{1}{G}: Rootwalla gets +2/+2 until end of turn. Activate only once each turn.', '{2}, Discard a card at random: Ogre Shaman deals 2 damage to any target.', '{2}: Create a 1/1 colorless Sliver creature token.', '{2}{W}: Creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.', '{3}, {T}: Choose a card name, then reveal a card at random from your hand. If that card has the chosen name, Cursed Scroll deals 2 damage to any target.', '{3}, {T}: Target player mills two cards. If two cards that share a color were milled this way, repeat this process.', '{5}, {T}: Draw two cards, then discard a card.', '{B}: Destroy target artifact, creature, or land you control.', '{G}, Discard a creature card: Search your library for a creature card, reveal that card, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', '{G}, {T}: Reveal cards from the top of your library until you reveal a basic land card. Put that card into your hand and all other cards revealed this way into your graveyard.', "{R}: Target creature can't be regenerated this turn.", '{T}, Discard a card at random: Mage il-Vec deals 1 damage to any target.', '{T}, Sacrifice Lotus Petal: Add one mana of any color.', '{T}, Sacrifice a Forest: Heartwood Giant deals 2 damage to target player or planeswalker.', '{T}, Sacrifice a creature: Destroy target nonblack creature.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}{B}, {T}: Put target creature card from your graveyard on top of your library.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{6}: Stalking Stones becomes a 3/3 Elemental artifact creature that's still a land. (This effect lasts indefinitely.)", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Wasteland: Destroy target nonbasic land.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {R}. Cinder Marsh doesn't untap during your next untap step.", "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {W}. Vec Townships doesn't untap during your next untap step.", "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {G}. Mogg Hollows doesn't untap during your next untap step.", "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {B}. Rootwater Depths doesn't untap during your next untap step.", "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {U}. Thalakos Lowlands doesn't untap during your next untap step.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Untap target attacking creature with shadow. Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt to and dealt by that creature this turn.', '{T}: Add {G}.\\n{1}: Add {R} or {W}.', '{T}: Choose a creature card name. Reveal the top four cards of your library and put all of them with that name into your hand. Put the rest into your graveyard.', "{T}: Destroy target artifact or creature. That permanent's controller gains control of Starke of Rath. (This effect lasts indefinitely.)", '{T}: Draw a card, then discard a card.', '{T}: Prevent the next 3 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.', '{T}: Rootwater Hunter deals 1 damage to any target.', '{T}: Until end of turn, target creature has base power 1 or base toughness 1.', '{U}: Killer Whale gains flying until end of turn.', '{W}, {T}: Tap target creature.']
flavor: ['"A jigsaw puzzle that lives, breeds, and thinks."\\n—Hanna, *Weatherlight* navigator', '"A perfect reflection of its world: brutal, fetal, and lacking truth."\\n—Oracle *en*-Vec', '"A skilled decoy can throw your enemies off your trail. A master decoy can survive to do it again."\\n—Gerrard of the Weatherlight', '"All dauthi are jackals, regardless of breed."\\n—Lyna, soltari emissary', '"As it moved, the wurm\'s spines gathered up bits of flowstone, which took the shapes of dead villagers\' heads. Each head spoke a single sound, but if taken together, they said, \'Alas for the living.\'"\\n—Dal myth of the wurm', '"Bitter water, vicious wave;\\nShadow-cold shallows, root-made maze.\\nHome\'s angry embrace."\\n—Rootwater Saga', '"Carrion! Keep your distance. My blade will come to you!"\\n—Crovax', '"Dauthi blood is soltari wine."\\n—Soltari Tales of Life', '"Every act of destruction has a repercussion."\\n—Karn, silver golem', '"Everything around here has cut a deal with gravity."\\n—Gerrard of the Weatherlight', '"Faugh!" snorted Tahngarth. "Why would it make a meal of something like you?" Squee looked relieved. "No," he continued, "you\'d make a much better toothpick."', '"Flying like a bird does not make you as free as one."\\n—Volrath', '"Forgive me," Mirri whispered. "I thought you a burden, and you saved my life." Hanna quietly accepted the apology.', '"Full of beauty and grace, with a predator\'s instincts . . . Although she wanders, I have always thought Mirri belongs in Llanowar most of all."\\n—Rofellos, Llanowar emissary', '"Gone today, here tomorrow."\\n—Ertai, wizard adept', '"Hard to imagine," mused Hanna, stroking the petal, "such a lovely flower inspiring such greed."', '"Here."', '"His tongue must be honey, the way he gathers ants to fight with him."\\n—Volrath', '"History is a potent weapon."\\n—Karn, silver golem', '"Hold your position! Leave doubt for the dying!"\\n—Tahngarth of the Weatherlight', '"Hope shall be the blade that severs our bonds."', '"Hup, two, three, four,\\nDunno how to count no more."\\n—Mogg march', '"I always charge a little extra to take on a pegasus. They fly like eagles, kick like mules, and hide like hermits."\\n—Tahli *en*-Dal, bounty hunter', '"I am confined by sleep and defined by nightmare."\\n—Crovax', '"I am light. I am dark. I must give my life to serve; not even death can release me."', '"I am reminded of the fable of the silver egg. Its owner cracks it open to see what jewels it holds, only to discover a simple yellow yolk."\\n—Karn, silver golem', '"I concede it was a cheap shot, but it was the only one I could afford."\\n—Gerrard of the Weatherlight', '"I followed her song only to find it was a dirge."\\n—Crovax', '"I got it! I got it! I—"', '"I hear the roaring of a wave whose waters are red and whose mists are black."\\n—Oracle *en*-Vec', '"I know to whom I owe the most loyalty, and I see him in the mirror every day."\\n—Starke', '"I used to describe something stable as \'rock solid.\' So much for that expression."\\n—Gerrard of the Weatherlight', '"I\'ll take that. You won\'t need it when the revolution comes."', '"If it tastes one drop of elvish blood I will cast it from the shroud to see it burn."\\n—Eladamri, Lord of Leaves', '"If there is such a thing as too much power, I have not discovered it."\\n—Volrath', '"If we cannot live proudly, we die so!"\\n—Eladamri, Lord of Leaves', '"In Barrin\'s name!" cried Lyna as Hanna\'s sword passed through her, "Ertai sends word that the portal is open—but not for long!"', '"In Rath," the priest said, "there is even greater need for prayer."', '"In times of war the victors rarely save their best for last."\\n—Gerrard of the Weatherlight', '"It is our duty to endure."\\n—Eladamri, Lord of Leaves', '"It is the nature of evil to turn you against yourself."\\n—Starke', '"It is the way of most wizards to begin by exiling themselves and to end by exiling everyone else."\\n—Hanna, *Weatherlight* navigator', '"It was probably a lousy spell in the first place."\\n—Ertai, wizard adept', '"It\'ll get us to the portal, but I can\'t guarantee what it\'ll do to the ship."\\n—Hanna, *Weatherlight* navigator', '"It\'s hard to hurt anyone when you\'re as transparent as your motives."\\n—Ertai, wizard adept', '"Just take a little off the top."', '"Just when I get them working, they always start fighting and tearing at each other for spare parts."\\n—Hanna, *Weatherlight* navigator', '"Let no child be without a sword. We will all fight, for if we fail, we will certainly all die."\\n—Oracle *en*-Vec', '"Let\'s do it again!"\\n—Squee, goblin cabin hand', '"Memory is a burden that wears at the soul as weather wears at stone."\\n—Crovax', '"Mine."', '"My enemies\' death yields threefold benefit: removal, reuse, and research."\\n—Volrath', '"My family sheltered in her light, the dark was content to wait."\\n—Crovax', '"My ship . . . ," Sisay mumbled. "Intact," Gerrard reassured her, "which is more than I can say for you, my friend." Sisay laughed despite the pain.', '"No home, no heart, no hope."\\n—Stronghold graffito', '"Not again."\\n—Hans', '"One cannot cleanse the wounds of failure."\\n—Karn, silver golem', '"One would think I would be accustomed to unexpected returns."\\n—Hanna, *Weatherlight* navigator', '"Only the most sophisticated inventions can survive nature\'s unsophisticated motivations."\\n—Hanna, *Weatherlight* navigator', '"Our belief shall be the lance that pierces Volrath\'s heart."', '"Part of me believes that Barrin taught me meditation simply to shut me up."\\n—Ertai, wizard adept', '"Peace will come, but whether born of harmony or entropy I cannot say."\\n—Oracle *en*-Vec', '"Prayer rarely explains."\\n—Orim, Samite healer', '"Rage is the only freedom left to me."', '"Relative of yours?" Ertai teased. Mirri simply sneered.', '"Remember the fable of the elf who came upon a cave of gold. In trying to free the largest piece, she was crushed by its weight."\\n—Karn, silver golem', '"See how you like it."\\n—Ertai, wizard adept', '"Sir, I just thought . . . ," explained Vhati. "Don\'t think," interrupted Greven. "It doesn\'t suit you."', '"Slivers are evil and slivers are sly; And if you get eaten, then no one will cry."\\n—Mogg children\'s rhyme', '"So like men are they: a hardened shell with fragile flesh beneath."\\n—Selenia, dark angel', '"Such fuss over machines, Gerrard. Remember that you are the prize of the Legacy. Throw away your toys!"\\n—Orim, Samite healer', '"Such rage," thought Vhati, gazing up at the thunderhead from the Predator. "It is Greven\'s mind manifest."', '"The cannon wasn\'t aimed at you!" pleaded Vhati. "I\'m not sure which is more pathetic," replied Greven, "your judgment or your aim."', '"The dauthi came from beneath the ruins one night, and the darkness cast them in the best possible light."\\n—Soltari Tales of Life', '"The fatal flaw in every plan is the assumption that you know more than your enemy."\\n—Volrath', '"The injury was being caught between this world and our own; the insult was to find walls within."\\n—Lyna, soltari emissary', '"The land promises nothing and keeps its promise."\\n—Oracle *en*-Vec', '"The silkworm spins itself a new existence. So the healer weaves the threads of life."\\n—Orim, Samite healer', '"There is nothing you can do that I cannot simply deny."\\n—Ertai, wizard adept', '"There shall be a vast shout and then a vaster silence."\\n—Oracle *en*-Vec', '"There\'s very little that escapes me, Greven. And you will escape very little if you fail."\\n—Volrath', '"These creatures offer new challenges in the scrutiny of entrails."\\n—Oracle *en*-Vec', '"They are called \'fowl\' for a reason."\\n—Mirri of the Weatherlight', '"They are convenient in having no souls, but less so in having no spirit."\\n—Volrath', '"They have knives for every soul."\\n—Lyna, soltari emissary', '"Those who fear the darkness have never seen what the light can do."\\n—Selenia, dark angel', '"To think that some find sleep a restful state."\\n—Volrath', '"Torahn\'s horns! They\'ve seen us. Now, statue, you must fight to save yourself!"\\n—Tahngarth, aboard the Predator', '"Twice I have let the Legacy slip away. Never again."\\n—Karn, silver golem', '"We are kinfolk," explained Karn to the sliver queen. "Just as you need your progeny to complete you, so do I need the pieces of the Legacy to make me whole."', '"We know our place in the cycle of life—and it is not as flies."\\n—Eladamri, Lord of Leaves', '"Where I come from, stone stays on the ground."\\n—Tahngarth of the Weatherlight', '"While we fought, the il surrendered."\\n—Oracle *en*-Vec', '"You see our world when you shut your eyes so tightly that tiny shapes float before them."\\n—Lyna, to Ertai', '"You want to know your enemy? Look at your feet while you trample him."\\n—Tahngarth of the Weatherlight', '"You will learn to earn death."\\n—Volrath', '"You\'ve got your childhood wish at last. Now you get to die."\\n—Gerrard, to Volrath', '"You\'ve not seen a storm until you\'ve seen the kind that roars between worlds."\\n—Lyna, soltari emissary', "A bristling wave of slivers broke against the Weatherlight's timbers.", 'A farewell to arms . . . and feet . . . and legs . . .', 'A full coffin is like a full coffer—both are attractive to thieves.', 'A hiss before dying.', 'A sickness stirs in its eyes, a nightmare born in darkened wails.', 'A snap of fingers, a snap of teeth.', 'After losing several of the devices to midair collisions, Greven forbade moggs from operating telethopters.', "All Mirri wanted to do was rest, but she couldn't ignore a nagging suspicion as she followed Crovax's skulking form.", 'As Gerrard made his escape, the wurm covered his flight by helping itself to three great mouthfuls of merfolk.', 'As the bough stretches, so shall you grow. As the roots spread, so shall you thrive.', 'As the sludge below began to shift and take shapes, Gerrard turned from the railing to Orim. "I suppose," he said, "it\'s a little too late for prayer, isn\'t it?"', 'Battles are won in nuance.', 'Bores ruin a party. Boars are party to ruin.', 'Bred as living shields, these slivers have proven unruly—they know they cannot be caught.', 'Burl, scurf, and bower\\nBirth fern and flower.', "Call it the thinking mage's version of brute force.", "Changing Rath's landscape is like tearing the scab from a wound.", "Cross the eyes of a hammerhead and you'll dot its teeth.", 'Death free throat from thirst, mouth from speech, feet from earth.\\n—Kor requiem', 'Each flower identical, every leaf and petal disturbingly exact.', 'Eating is all it knows.', "For a sharp second, Selenia froze, and Crovax's blade found home. As the angel shattered like glass, Crovax felt his mind collapse—the curse had been fulfilled.", 'From its maw comes neither word nor whisper—only wind.', 'From nothing came teeth.', 'Frozen by conscience, Karn did not resist as the moggs carried him to the Predator.', 'Furnace air crackles with magmatic cackles.', 'Gerrard grinned and drew his sword. "This won\'t be a fair fight," he called to his crew. "They should have brought a second ship!"', 'Greven *il*-Vec lifted Vhati off his feet. "The fall will give you time to think on your failure."', 'Hanna: "We must learn how they protect each other."\\nMirri: "After they\'re done trying to kill us, all right?"', 'Her children are ever part of her.', 'Hope is the one crop that can grow in any climate.', 'Hope of deliverance is scorched by the fire of futility.', 'Hunger is like the sea: deep, endless, and unforgiving.', 'If dragons excel at anything more than vanity, it is greed.', "If you try to sneak up on a rootwalla, you'll suddenly find yourself dealing with twice the lizard.", 'In the depths of Rootwater, salvage and sewage differ only in texture.', 'It is like life and destiny: we think we know the story, but we have read only half the tale.', 'It is said that the wind will blow the world past if you wait long enough.', "It was not the minotaur's shoulders but his soul that bore the heaviest weight.", 'Life has always been a dance. It is only fitting that death sing the tune.', 'Living below a flowstone foundry produces a disproportionate number of fire mages among the il.', 'Mirri did not have time to think, only to react.', 'Mogglings have been known to play ball with hibernating slivers, completely unaware of their true nature.', 'Most creatures grow out of their baby teeth, but sabertooth wyverns grow into theirs.', 'Ogre shamans must be bright enough to learn their invocations and dim enough to use them.', 'Once these horrifying creatures were perfected, there was no need for armodons.', 'One mogg to aim the catapult, one mogg to steer the rock.', 'Only a matter as vital as destroying Volrath could bring together the reclusive kor people.', 'Only by sacrificing any semblance of defense could Gerrard best Greven.', 'Only the warrior who can admit mortal weakness will be bolstered by immortal strength.', 'Orim regarded Gerrard coolly. "You are like the drake," she said, her expression unchanging. "It works hard to maintain its position, but to us it seems to glide along effortlessly. You must do the same."', 'Rath forces plants from its surface as one presses whey from cheese.', 'Seeking the company of plants ensures that your wits will go to seed.', 'Shackles of gold are still shackles.', 'Spans of spines leapt from one sliver to the next, forming a deadly hedge around the Weatherlight.', 'Squee bounced up and down. "I sees a horsey, an\' a piggy, an\' a—"\\n"If you don\'t shut up," hissed Mirri, "you\'ll see a kidney and a spleeny."', 'Squee tucked the warm ball in his pocket and slipped a pebble in its place. "Glok," he mumbled, and hid.', 'Stand clear if he gets an itch.', 'Takara shook with guilt. She knew the last image her father had seen was her sword flashing toward him.', 'The *Weatherlight* dragged the Predator behind it, the cradle hauling the casket.', 'The air was filled with the cracks and snaps of flesh hardening as the new sliver joined the battle.', 'The assassin sees only throats and hears only heartbeats.', 'The bite of the tinviper feels most like a razor drawn across the tongue.', 'The ceiling and the floor fell in love, but only the wall knew.\\n—Dal saying', 'The elves and merfolk have nothing but bitterness for each other. The trolls, however, find them both rather tasty.', 'The first sliver burst against the cave wall, and others piled in behind to deepen the new tunnel.', "The hounds' barks are a horrifying chorus of screams, moans, and whispers.", 'The hunter would never forget the time or place where he first met the carnassid, for they buried him there.', 'The kor forsake roots for the winding of the path, forsake voices for the silence of the mind, forsake all else for the poverty of isolation.', 'The less you have, the harder you fight for it.', 'The rain is driven like nails.', "The seed of a world's evil.", 'The swarm seemed unmoved by the artificial slivers\' destruction. "They clearly were not the leaders," Hanna cursed. "I guess we\'ll have to do this the hard way."', 'The true treasure no thief can touch.', 'These are its last days. Better to grow broad and heavy. Better that the enemy is crushed beneath its carcass.', 'These are its last days. It is doomed to be remembered only until the hunters hunger again.', 'They drift in and out of shadow and ever on toward madness.', "They'll attack whatever's in front of them—as long as you tell them where that is.", 'To snare what lies between worlds takes the patient reach of trees.', 'Two things are needed to survive the harsh skies of Rath: a thick hide and a thicker skull.', 'Unlike their cousins, Rathi basilisks turn their victims into puddles of flowstone.', 'Water is life. Or perhaps it is just something to wash it down with.', 'What is high as a mountain and low as a snake?\\n—Dal riddle', "When the clever counterfeit was accepted by the hive, Volrath's influence upon the slivers grew even stronger.", "Wind in the trees is soothing, but the same can't be said for trees on the wind.", 'Within without.', 'Wrap the flame as twine, Kingdoms will be thine.']
artist: ['Adam Rex', 'Allen Williams', 'Andrew Robinson', 'Anthony S. Waters', 'April Lee', 'Brian Snõddy', 'Brom', 'Charles Gillespie', 'Christopher Rush', 'Ciruelo', 'Colin MacNeil', 'D. Alexander Gregory', 'Dan Frazier', 'Daniel Gelon', 'Daren Bader', 'Dermot Power', 'DiTerlizzi', 'Donato Giancola', 'Doug Chaffee', 'Douglas Shuler', 'Drew Tucker', 'Eric David Anderson', 'Gary Leach', 'Greg Simanson', 'Hannibal King', 'Heather Hudson', 'Janet Aulisio', 'Jason Alexander Behnke', 'Jeff A. Menges', 'Jeff Laubenstein', 'Jeff Miracola', 'Jim Nelson', 'Joel Biske', 'John Matson', 'Kaja Foglio', 'Keith Parkinson', 'Ken Meyer, Jr.', 'Kev Walker', 'M. W. Kaluta & DiTerlizzi', 'Margaret Organ-Kean', 'Mark Poole', 'Mark Zug', 'Matthew D. Wilson', 'Mike Raabe', 'Paolo Parente', 'Pete Venters', 'Phil Foglio', 'Quinton Hoover', 'Randy Elliott', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Rebecca Guay', 'Richard Kane Ferguson', 'Richard Thomas', 'Robert Bliss', 'Roger Raupp', 'Ron Spencer', 'Scott Kirschner', 'Scott M. Fischer', 'Stephen Daniele', 'Steve Luke', 'Susan Van Camp', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Thomas M. Baxa', 'Tom Kyffin', 'Tom Wänerstrand', 'Una Fricker', 'Val Mayerik', 'Zina Saunders', 'rk post']
